  "text" : {
    "status" : "generated",
    "div" : "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Generated Narrative: ActorDefinition PHCoreClient</b></p><a name=\"PHCoreClient\"> </a><a name=\"hcPHCoreClient\"> </a><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td><b>Actor: PHCoreClient </b></td><td>PH Core Client</td><td>Type: system </td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"3\"><div><p>A PH Core Client initiates FHIR API requests to access or exchange PH Core resources. It correctly handles resources received in responses. When it produces resources for a supported write interaction, it fulfills the applicable population obligations. A read-only client is not required to author resource payloads. The role applies to the request being initiated; a system may also act as a PH Core Server in other exchanges. The API requirements are defined in the <a href=\"CapabilityStatement-PHCoreClientCapabilityStatement.html\">PH Core Client CapabilityStatement</a>.</p>\n</div></td></tr></table></div>"
